data.content:
Your code **does not use `Thread.Abort`**, `Thread.ResetAbort`, or catch `ThreadAbortException`. The APIs it does use (`Thread.Start`, `Thread.Join`, `Thread.Sleep`) work identically in .NET 8 — no migration is needed for abort-related concerns.

**However**, for a modern .NET 8 idiomatic rewrite, consider replacing manual threads with `Parallel.ForEach` or `Task.WhenAll` with cooperative cancellation via `CancellationToken`:

```csharp
public async Task RunBatchAsync(List<WorkItem> items, CancellationToken ct = default)
{
    await Parallel.ForEachAsync(items, ct, async (item, token) =>
    {
        token.ThrowIfCancellationRequested();
        await Task.Delay(100, token); // replaces Thread.Sleep
        item.Result = ComputeResult(item.Input);
    });
}
```

This gives you safe, cooperative cancellation without ever needing `Thread.Abort`.
